== Fetched at install time, from pinned upstream versions (not vendored) ==
- Inter, Montserrat, Bebas Neue, Instrument Serif, Anton, GFS Didot,
  JetBrains Mono, Barlow Condensed — SIL Open Font License 1.1. Downloaded
  with consent and pinned hashes into .kit/fonts/.
- GSAP — GreenSock / Webflow, GSAP Standard License (non-OSI). Downloaded at
  install time with its license header intact, only if a module needs it.
- HyperFrames — HeyGen, Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes
- agent-reach — upstream author, license per upstream.
- last30days — upstream author, license per upstream.
- humanizer — upstream author, license per upstream (includes material
  derived from CC BY-SA sources; never relicensed here).
- defuddle — upstream author, license per upstream.
- OpenMontage — upstream project, license per upstream.
- Remotion — Remotion AG, Remotion License (company tier may require a paid
  license).
- ponytail, karpathy-skills, superpowers —
  optional plugins, installed by the user from upstream, licenses per upstream.
- Playwright (Microsoft, Apache-2.0) and its browser builds, downloaded from
  Playwright's official CDN over HTTPS and integrity-checked by Playwright.
- Whisper (OpenAI, MIT), faster-whisper (SYSTRAN, MIT), OpenCV (Apache-2.0),
  librosa (ISC) — installed from package indexes with pinned hashes.

== Invoked as external programs (never vendored) ==
- FFmpeg — LGPL/GPL, installed by the user.
- git, Python, Node.js — installed by the user.

== Third-party services ==
Paid APIs and apps (voice, image and video generation, scraping, scheduling,
Adobe apps, AI coding agents) are used only through the user's own accounts
and are governed by each vendor's terms of service.
